#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
STEP 7A — CLINICAL QUERY ENGINE v1
====================================
This file is the standalone ClinicalQueryEngine imported by the Patient RAG
Pipeline (step7a_patient_pipeline_v3.2.py). Place it at /content/ and the
pipeline bootstrap will import it automatically.

ARCHITECTURE:
  Layer 0 — Intent classifier    : catches vague/OOS queries before Pinecone
  Layer 1 — Synonym expansion    : normalises lay terms to clinical equivalents
  Layer 2 — Specialty router     : attaches derm-only filter to query
  Layer 3 — HyDE generation      : generates hypothetical answer to improve recall
  Layer 4 — Pinecone retrieval   : dual-vector (raw + HyDE blend) with filter
  Layer 5 — Context recall check : re-queries without filter if <2 results
  Layer 6 — Cross-encoder rerank : pure rerank-score sort (no cosine blend)
  Layer 7 — Graph expansion      : fetches sibling/parent chunks for context

FIXES vs inline engine in pipeline v3.2:
  FIX 1 — Synonym expansion before embed
    Raw queries like "sebderm", "skin purging", "bacne", "fine lines",
    "mask" were hitting Pinecone as-is and scoring below threshold.
    Now expanded to full clinical equivalents before embedding.

  FIX 2 — Vague query guard
    Queries like "Please help me" / "help" no longer hit Pinecone.
    Returns a structured clarification prompt instead.

  FIX 3 — Specialty router
    Derm queries get a Pinecone metadata filter {specialty: dermatology}
    applied automatically. Non-derm queries get appropriate specialty scoping.
    Prevents hepatology/pathology docs polluting derm answers.

  FIX 4 — Recall fallback
    If specialty-filtered retrieval returns <2 results, automatically
    re-queries without the filter using a relaxed threshold.

  FIX 5 — Pure rerank sort
    Previous cosine blend (0.45 cosine + 0.55 rerank) actively harmed
    chunks with negative rerank scores. Now sorts purely by rerank score.
    Cosine is only used as a tiebreaker when rerank is unavailable.

  FIX 6 — Concept-filtered retrieval
    If the query maps to a known FEA concept, performs a concept-anchored
    retrieval pass using concept_ids metadata filter, merged with semantic
    retrieval for maximum recall.

RESULT TYPE:
  RetrievalResult dataclass — compatible with the pipeline's
  _engine_query_to_chunks() normaliser which handles both this and the
  inline dict format.
"""

